{
  "schema": 29,
  "id": "klon-bypass-v1",
  "name": "Bypass · Klon, true or buffered (3PDT switch + 3PDT footswitch)",
  "version": {
    "major": 1,
    "minor": 1
  },
  "description": "The Klon KTR's bypass, after Aion FX's Refractor: a 3PDT on-on (SW1, slide or toggle; Aion fits a 4PDT slide with one pole unused) picks Buffered or True bypass, a 3PDT footswitch (SW2) switches the effect and lights the LED. Buffered: your circuit's input buffer always runs, and when bypassed its output (buffer, through C2 and R4) goes to the jack. True bypass: in goes straight to out. R26, R27 and R28 hold the unused output at ground so switching doesn't pop; bypassed in Buffered, R27 lets a little of the effect through, as Aion draws it. Wire send to your circuit's input, return to its output and buffer to its input buffer's output. Flip both in Knobs.",
  "tags": [
    "bypass",
    "buffer",
    "footswitch",
    "switching",
    "klon"
  ],
