  "notes": {
    "part:C2": "With R4, the buffered output: the input buffer's signal for the bypass board, used when bypassed in Buffered mode. R3 keeps C2 charged so switching doesn't pop.",
    "part:SW1A": "Bypass mode: Buffered or True bypass. Any 3PDT on-on, slide or toggle; Aion fits a 4PDT slide (E-Switch EG4208) with one pole unused. Aion's lugs 1-9 are A1-C3 here.",
    "part:SW2A": "The 3PDT footswitch (Aion's FSA and FSC; B lights the LED). Lug 1 is On here, so Aion's A1/A3 and C1/C3 trade names.",
    "part:R26": "R26 and R27 tie the unused output (the buffer's or the effect's) to R28, which holds it at ground so the footswitch doesn't pop. As Aion draws it (and as the original's R243, the same 68k): bypassed in Buffered, R27 lets the effect into the output about 22 dB under the dry signal at noon."
  }
